{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1092404-setting-up-my-first-mage-game","id":1092404,"title":"Setting up my First Mage Game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-14T11:47:08-07:00","id":1092404,"title":"Setting up my First Mage Game","content":"I am putting together my first Mage Game, we usually play Vampire. We are taking the option from the chroniclers guide of a &quot;pathless&quot; game where Arcana can only be increased by a mentor with that level as there is no connection to the higher realms. We're also saying any Arcane experience can also be used without a mentor.<br /> <br /> How or what would be the best way to make these mentor tutor sessions more then just down time sessions at the completion of a story earning the mentors teaching. I'd like to make it more then, &quot;ok the older mage agrees and you spend the next six weeks studying, now you have forces 4&quot; <br /> <br /> Suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T13:12:56-07:00","id":1092451,"title":"","content":"There's no teacher like experience, and any Mage mentor worth his Gnosis knows this. Depending on which Order your players are, this could take make forms.<br /> <br /> For an AA, the mentor may arrange for a long campaign with expected (or arranged!) obstacles, or a Mysterium mage could spend time wandering thru the maze of her Oneiros, her mentor setting her learning exercises. A breakdown of what the play did and should have done in certain scenarios is a good way for a mentor to give some hands-on learning. All of the Orders have a way to get into the &quot;field&quot; and get some tried and true experiences that teach their students. And remember, the best mentors are those that use those experiences to further their own aims as well as teach their students. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5202-hotchepsoot","name":"HotChepSoot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T15:05:12-07:00","id":1092525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kevorkiandoctor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1092404-setting-up-my-first-mage-game#post1092404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am putting together my first Mage Game, we usually play Vampire. We are taking the option from the chroniclers guide of a &quot;pathless&quot; game where Arcana can only be increased by a mentor with that level as there is no connection to the higher realms. We're also saying any Arcane experience can also be used without a mentor.<br /> <br /> How or what would be the best way to make these mentor tutor sessions more then just down time sessions at the completion of a story earning the mentors teaching. I'd like to make it more then, &quot;ok the older mage agrees and you spend the next six weeks studying, now you have forces 4&quot;<br /> <br /> Suggestions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's a couple of questions to get you thinking:<br /> <br /> 1: What's the role of mysteries if understanding them doesn't increase your understanding of the arcana? Addiction to mysteries is THE theme of Mage, and solving said mysteries is one of the primary ways (if not THE primary way) for mages to increase their understanding and skill in the arcana.<br /> <br /> 2. If you can only increase your understanding by learning from a tutor and not on your own (which is incredibly un-human, by the way), how did the first mage(s) increase his (their) understanding of the arcana?<br /> <br /> Neither question is meant to give disrespect towards your decision, but given that you're starting your first game in a VERY non-basic game I felt that they were pertinent. Changing basic things about the setting causes dramatic shifts in the entire setting as well as game play. I would personally recommend that you stick with the base game before altering it if you haven't played it before. That way you have a stronger grasp of how the game was intended to play such that you have a better idea of how you can change things to suit your own style.<br /> <br /> Edit: To answer your question, I would alter your decision slightly and say that you can still learn the arcana on your own, but it's faster, easier, safer, and/or cheaper to learn from tutors. This way people can still have their pathless mages and can also still go out and study on their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","user":"Falcon777","date":". 05-14-2017, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T16:14:17-07:00","id":1092564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1092404-setting-up-my-first-mage-game?p=1092525#post1092525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1: What's the role of mysteries if understanding them doesn't increase your understanding of the arcana? Addiction to mysteries is THE theme of Mage, and solving said mysteries is one of the primary ways (if not THE primary way) for mages to increase their understanding and skill in the arcana.<br /> <br /> 2. If you can only increase your understanding by learning from a tutor and not on your own (which is incredibly un-human, by the way), how did the first mage(s) increase his (their) understanding of the arcana?</div> </div> </div> </div>They did say that AXP can be spent without a mentor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T18:25:39-07:00","id":1092600,"title":"","content":"Ah, my bad, thought I saw cannot instead of can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T01:46:43-07:00","id":1092698,"title":"","content":"If this isn't a discussion you're interested in having, I'll leave the thread alone, but have you considered running Mage as written instead of applying 1E hacks to 2E when you haven't actually played it yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T11:16:44-07:00","id":1092877,"title":"","content":"The only change I decided for XP was that only AXP can be spent on Gnosis and Arcana as it will slow progression down a little and I believe it will result in more well-rounded characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T15:47:15-07:00","id":1092997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1092404-setting-up-my-first-mage-game?p=1092698#post1092698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If this isn't a discussion you're interested in having, I'll leave the thread alone, but have you considered running Mage as written instead of applying 1E hacks to 2E when you haven't actually played it yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am waiting on my 2ed book, so far all my material is 1ed, but of course I'm open to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T01:16:44-07:00","id":1093145,"title":"","content":"What's your goal with eliminating paths? What perceived problem are you trying to eliminate?<br /> <br /> Is it a matter of wanting to allow any Arcana spread? With heavy-handed (in 1E) enforcement of the Path stereotypes? Issues with the Supernal as presented, looking for a more traditional magical experience? All of the above, or something else entirely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 05-16-2017, 04:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T10:40:33-07:00","id":1093325,"title":"","content":"Have you decided what kind of people their Mentors are? The personality of the teacher will be reflected in the type of the lesson.<br /> <br /> Once you figure this out, look at the Spells available under the studied Arcanum rating. Keeping with your example - Forces 4 has &quot;Transform Energy&quot;. A musically-inclined Mage can set up singing Tesla coils, so the student can watch them under Mage Sight and try to replicate the effect. This kind of lesson is pleasant for everyone involved, and can end in trying out different music pieces. A hard-core kind of teacher can chain their student and repeatedly send electric jolts through the metal, until the pupil is motivated enough to succeed.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.jim-butcher.com/books/dresden/small-favor/small-favor-chapter-1\" target=\"_blank\">You can find another example under this link.</a><br /> <br /> If you or your players decided what their Mentors are like, you can try sharing that on the Forums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T04:30:58-07:00","id":1093610,"title":"","content":"Acanthus<br /> Students on the Path of Thistle must solve a cause-and-effect dilemma. Like being presented a button that will save a loved one from certain death, while simultaneously killing some random person. (There was a movie about this but the title escapes me.) Similarly, the PC must outsmart a member of the Gentry through cunning or guile.<br /> <br /> Mastigos<br /> The mentor is highly antagonistic , and subjects the PC to a nightmarish waking dream they must escape from. Perhaps it's a twisted, Silent Hill-type version of the PC's hometown. Perhaps they are sent to stop a serial killer who turns out to be their a living embodiment of their sins.<br /> <br /> Moros<br /> The Leaden Coin apprentice must traverse the underworld to speak with the ghost of a powerful sage (think Tiresias of Greek mythology), or map out a City of the Dead at the edge if reality. Alternately she might be asked to frequent nursing homes, taking lives of those ready to embrace their deaths. A master could also charge her with crafting a rare and exquisite gem, only to destroy it afterwards.<br /> <br /> Obrimos<br /> The Path of the Mighty grants revelations that allow a theurgist to discern truths from falsehoods. He might use Prime to manipulate a magical puzzle artifact (like the game The Room), or answer esoteric riddles from a sphinx-like cherubim.<br /> <br /> Thyrsus<br /> Eat or be eaten: The new Shaman is abandoned in a jungle with nothing but wits and a knife. He may have to search for a rare medicinal plant guarded by hostile spirits, or entrusted with a dangerous diplomatic mission to the Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4260,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","user":"terpsichordean","date":". 05-17-2017, 07:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}